# Copy to ".env.local" for local dev (never commit .env.local).
# In production, set variables in Railway → Service → Variables (not in git).
#
# FRONTEND vs SERVER
# -----------------
# • "Frontend env" in Next.js = any name starting with NEXT_PUBLIC_
#   Those values are inlined into the JavaScript sent to the browser — treat them as WORLD-READABLE.
#   Never put OpenAI keys, webhook secrets, or service_role keys in NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# • Variables WITHOUT that prefix are server-only (API routes, Server Components, middleware).
#   OPENAI_API_KEY and SHYNVO_* URLs live here; the browser never sees them.
# • Copilot: the browser only calls same-origin paths like /api/copilot/chat; the server reads OPENAI_API_KEY.

# --- NEXT_PUBLIC_* (browser / frontend — non-secrets only) ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://shynvo.app
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL=https://your-store.lemonsqueezy.com/checkout/...
# Optional: where Copilot POSTs (default /api/copilot/chat). Change only if you want the UI to hit /api/reasoning/... instead.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COPILOT_PROXY_PATH=/api/reasoning/v1/chat

# --- Server-only secrets (never NEXT_PUBLIC_) ---
# OpenAI: used only inside /api/copilot/chat — NOT available on the frontend
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Webhook signing secret from Lemon Squeezy (rotate if it was ever committed).
LEMONSQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# --- Linked services (server only — no NEXT_PUBLIC_) ---
# Proxies: GET /api/reasoning/health → {REASONING_URL}/health , GET /api/robot/docs → {ROBOT}/docs
# SHYNVO_REASONING_API_URL=https://your-reasoning-service.up.railway.app
# SHYNVO_ROBOT_API_URL=https://your-automation-service.up.railway.app
SHYNVO_REASONING_API_URL=
SHYNVO_ROBOT_API_URL=

# --- Supabase (auth — set both for sign-in / protected console; omit both to skip auth locally) ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=  # server only — required for Lemon webhook → subscriptions upsert
